    description: "Three defects in scripts/measure-taint-precision.py's packet subcommand, all\nfound by refuters reading measurement 0012's rendered packets against source.\nNone changed a label; each is a way the packet misleads a reader.\n\n1. A SINK SITE MATCHED INSIDE A BLOCK COMMENT. The tmux packet lists\n   compat/imsg-buffer.c:813 as a sendmsg call site. Line 813 is comment text\n   -- \" * assumption: fd got sent if sendmsg sent anything\" -- inside a /* */\n   opened at 812. `scrub` blanks LINE comments and string interiors; it does\n   not track multi-line block comments, so every continuation line of a C-style\n   block comment is searched as code. This is defect 1 from 0006 section F\n   (\"matches sink names as bare SUBSTRINGS ... inside a quoted pattern\")\n   returning through the one comment form scrub does not model.\n\n2. A WHOLE-FILE PSEUDO-SYMBOL DOUBLE-ATTRIBUTES SITES. ArkLib :3 and :5 list\n   the same open() sites twice: once under the real enclosing function\n   (revert_nav 5-84) and once under a module-level symbol printed as\n   `in file (scripts/revert_nav.py 1-93)`. Module-level execution never reaches\n   those calls; the whole-file span contains them TEXTUALLY, not as a body.\n   In :3 the pseudo-symbol is even named `file`, colliding with a loop variable\n   of the same name on line 26.\n\n3. BASH_SOURCE LISTED AS AN ENVIRONMENT READ SITE. The cert-manager packet\n   lists checkhash.sh:21 (SCRIPT_DIR=\"$( cd \"$( dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\" )\"\n   ...)\") among the SOURCE sites for a source typed environ (env_read).\n   BASH_SOURCE is a bash-internal special array, never exported. hypergumbo\n   ITSELF stopped emitting it as an env read (INV-nular, PR #541); the packet\n   builder's own shell_env_sites has not followed, so the instrument now\n   asserts something the tool under measurement no longer does.\n\nItem 3 is the pointed one: the builder was put in-repo precisely so its defects\ncould be fixed rather than re-encountered, and it has now drifted away from the\nproduction catalogue it is supposed to illustrate. Its _SHELL_NON_ENV set is a\nsecond home for a fact bash.py already owns."  # 90f3
    fields: {}  # 90f3
- op: discuss  # 3d87
  at: '2026-09-25T18:02:50Z'  # 3d87
  by: agent  # 3d87
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3d87
  clock: 2  # 3d87
  nonce: 3d87  # 3d87
  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-09-25 (dev e4a47383ab). DEFECT 1 IS DECLINED IN CODE, NOT ON THIS ROW. Status unchanged.\n\nscripts/measure-taint-precision.py (~line 779, the `_COMMENT_OPENERS` comment) reads: \"Block comments are deliberately NOT handled: doing it correctly needs a lexer, and doing it by regex across 16 languages would trade a known limitation for an unknown one. A block comment therefore still yields candidate lines, which errs toward showing the adjudicator too much rather than too little.\"\n\nThat is a refusal of this row's defect 1 (tmux compat/imsg-buffer.c:813 matched inside a /* */), recorded only as a code comment. Either this row adopts it (re-scope to defects 2 and 3, with defect 1 declined and the reason above), or the owner overrules it. Defects 2 (whole-file pseudo-symbol double-attribution) and 3 (BASH_SOURCE as an env read) were NOT re-checked in this review."  # 3d87
- op: discuss  # 5424
  at: '2026-10-01T00:56:57Z'  # 5424
  by: agent  # 5424
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5424
  clock: 3  # 5424
  nonce: '5424'  # 5424
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES. All three defects reproduce on the current builder; defect 1 is declined in a code comment.\n\nscripts/measure-taint-precision.py has not changed in this area since 7d8b675c4d (2026-09-09). I loaded the module through importlib and called its functions directly.\n\n- Defect 1: find_sites(['int f() {','  /* start','   * fd got sent if sendmsg sent anything','   */','  sendmsg(fd);','}'], ['sendmsg'], 1, 6, 'c') returns line 3, the comment line, as well as line 5. The refusal comment sits at lines 779-783 (\"Block comments are deliberately NOT handled ...\"). It comes from 8f1a240b0e (2026-09-02), the day BEFORE this row was filed, so the row was filed against an already-recorded refusal.\n- Defect 2: sink_search_spans({'path': ['python:scripts/revert_nav.py:1-1:file:file', 'python:scripts/revert_nav.py:5-84:revert_nav:function']}) returns [('scripts/revert_nav.py', 1, -1, 'file'), ('scripts/revert_nav.py', 5, 84, 'revert_nav')]. The file span (lines 908-911, widened to the whole file at render time, around 1141) is searched separately, so every site inside revert_nav is listed twice. No de-duplication against the function spans.\n- Defect 3: shell_env_sites on the checkhash.sh line returns (2, 'SCRIPT_DIR=\"$( cd \"$( dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\" )\" ...'). _SHELL_NON_ENV (line 920) is still \"0123456789@*#?$!-_\". bash.py:276-289 owns _SHELL_STATE_NAMES, which includes BASH_SOURCE, and the builder does not import it. The divergence the row names is unchanged.\n\nProposed item change, as the 2026-09-25 entry already suggested: re-scope to defects 2 and 3, recording defect 1 as declined (reason at lines 779-783) unless the owner overrules. For defect 3, the fix shape is to import bash.py's set rather than extend the local copy (one home for the fact)."  # 5424
- op: update  # 3319
