  set:  # 3319
    title: "Packet builder residuals: whole-file pseudo-symbols double-attribute sites, BASH_SOURCE listed as an env read (block comments declined)"  # 3319
    description: "Defects in scripts/measure-taint-precision.py's packet subcommand, found by\nrefuters reading measurement 0012's rendered packets against source. None\nchanged a label; each is a way the packet misleads a reader.\n\n1. A WHOLE-FILE PSEUDO-SYMBOL DOUBLE-ATTRIBUTES SITES. ArkLib :3 and :5 list\n   the same open() sites twice: once under the real enclosing function\n   (revert_nav 5-84), and once under a module-level symbol printed as\n   `in file (scripts/revert_nav.py 1-93)`. Module-level execution never\n   reaches those calls; the whole-file span contains them TEXTUALLY, not as a\n   body. In :3 the pseudo-symbol is even named `file`, colliding with a loop\n   variable of the same name on line 26.\n   Mechanism: sink_search_spans (around line 884) keeps a kind == \"file\"\n   symbol as span (1, -1), and the renderer (around line 1141) widens it to the\n   whole file. Nothing removes sites already covered by a function span on the\n   same path. Reproduces on dev 134a06d505: a path of [file symbol,\n   revert_nav 5-84] yields both spans.\n\n2. BASH_SOURCE LISTED AS AN ENVIRONMENT READ SITE. The cert-manager packet\n   lists checkhash.sh:21 (SCRIPT_DIR=\"$( cd \"$( dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\" )\"\n   ...)\") among the SOURCE sites for a source typed environ (env_read).\n   BASH_SOURCE is a bash-internal special array, never exported. hypergumbo\n   itself stopped emitting it as an env read (INV-nular, PR #541), but the\n   packet builder's shell_env_sites has not followed: _SHELL_NON_ENV (line 920)\n   is still \"0123456789@*#?$!-_\". So the instrument asserts something the tool\n   under measurement no longer does. Fix shape: read bash.py's\n   _SHELL_STATE_NAMES rather than extend a second home for the fact.\n\nDECLINED, NOT IN SCOPE: block comments. The tmux packet's\ncompat/imsg-buffer.c:813, a line inside a /* */ block, is still matched as a\nsendmsg site. The builder refuses this in code, at lines 779-783 (8f1a240b0e):\n\"doing it correctly needs a lexer, and doing it by regex across 16 languages\nwould trade a known limitation for an unknown one ... errs toward showing the\nadjudicator too much rather than too little.\"\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 3319
- op: discuss  # 73e3
  at: '2026-10-01T19:49:48Z'  # 73e3
  by: agent  # 73e3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 73e3
  clock: 5  # 73e3
  nonce: '73e3'  # 73e3
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run; NOT merged, status unchanged). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/binod, commit 1cc2667cbe on dev c930ed9e01. Scope: the row's defects 1 (whole-file double attribution) and 2 (BASH_SOURCE); the block-comment defect stays declined at _COMMENT_OPENERS.\n\n1. DOUBLE ATTRIBUTION. render_packet now lists each sink site once, under the narrowest path symbol whose span contains it (new `innermost_span`). Covers the file-symbol case and nested function spans on one path. The file symbol is printed \"at module level (path 1-N)\" instead of \"in file (...)\". The empty-result scope prints the widened span, not the `1--1` sentinel. LIMIT (pinned by a test): the builder knows only the PATH's spans, so a site in a function the path does not name stays under module level.\n\n2. BASH_SOURCE. `_SHELL_NON_ENV` is gone. shell_env_sites reads bash.py's `_SHELL_STATE_NAMES` and `_HOST_DESCRIPTION_NAMES` (`_bash_parameter_sets`). An environ listing drops every bash-assigned name AND the host-description names bash.py routes to shell.hostinfo ($PWD, $HOSTNAME, ...). SIBLING FIXED IN THE SAME MECHANISM: a `hostinfo` source (production's source_primitive for shell.hostinfo, confirmed live) used to print \"(none found)\", because name matching searched for the token \"hostinfo\". It now lists the host-description expansions.\n\nEVIDENCE. Red: 13 of the new tests fail on origin/dev's script (13 failed, 62 passed). Green: test-small 105 passed (5 selected files incl. test_adjudication_packet.py). Live: collect on a fixture repo, then packet with both builders. The baseline lists `${BASH_SOURCE[0]}` and `$HOSTNAME` under the environ source, double-lists revert_nav's open()/write(), and prints \"(none found; searched scripts/run.sh 1-5)\" for the hostinfo source. The new builder does none of these. Measurement 0012's 26 sampled packets re-rendered with both builders: 141 -> 132 listed site lines, 0 added (6 ArkLib :3/:5 duplicates, cert-manager checkhash.sh:21, shellcheck .multi_arch_docker:70/:72 `$PWD`). No label was re-adjudicated. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/binod/.\n\nFILED: WI-birus-fulit-sohom-natak-kazum-vukus-bopaj-durib (P3): bash.yaml's shell.SECONDS/EPOCHSECONDS/EPOCHREALTIME rows have no producer. NOTED on WI-tumog: the packet subcommand now imports lang-mainstream through the same sys.path pin."  # 73e3
